WEBVTT

1
00:01:08.365 --> 00:01:11.310
<i>What would home look like?</i>

2
00:01:11.335 --> 00:01:13.302
<i>I don't know.</i>

3
00:01:15.805 --> 00:01:19.151
<i>A farmhouse in the
valley, I guess,</i>

4
00:01:19.176 --> 00:01:22.811
<i>like the one we grew
up in, Liza and I.</i>

5
00:01:34.758 --> 00:01:36.869
I remember hiding in
the orchard at night.

6
00:01:36.894 --> 00:01:39.871
Looking down at the
lighted windows,

7
00:01:39.896 --> 00:01:42.007
waiting for our daddy
to fall asleep,

8
00:01:42.032 --> 00:01:45.076
just so we could
go back inside.

9
00:01:45.101 --> 00:01:47.001
Do you remember that, Liza?

10
00:01:48.404 --> 00:01:51.783
Hmm? Do you remember that?

11
00:01:51.808 --> 00:01:53.785
I'd imagine him passing out.

12
00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:55.987
With one of his lucky
strikes in his hand,

13
00:01:56.012 --> 00:01:58.923
the house catching fire,

14
00:01:58.948 --> 00:02:02.850
the orchard, the whole
valley burning up.

15
00:02:06.088 --> 00:02:07.932
So, how does it feel, Liza?

16
00:02:07.957 --> 00:02:10.335
Your first big score?

17
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.339
I don't know. Excited, nervous,

18
00:02:14.364 --> 00:02:17.308
like I'm spying on someone,

19
00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:18.977
someone doing something dirty.

20
00:02:19.002 --> 00:02:20.745
Yeah.

21
00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:22.914
I know what you mean.

22
00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:24.015
Shame.

23
00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.384
It's all right, little sis.

24
00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:29.177
It's a good sign when
you feel a little bad.

25
00:02:58.439 --> 00:03:01.752
<i>Liza? Liza, can you hear me?</i>

26
00:03:01.777 --> 00:03:03.487
<i>Liza?</i>

27
00:03:03.512 --> 00:03:06.090
I can hear you.

28
00:03:06.115 --> 00:03:08.158
Are you in pain?

29
00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:10.494
No. I think I'm all right.

30
00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:12.362
<i>Theo?</i>

31
00:03:12.387 --> 00:03:17.357
<i>Theo should've worn his safety belt.
Shit.</i>

32
00:04:05.038 --> 00:04:08.017
Liza, can you move?

33
00:04:08.042 --> 00:04:09.418
I think so.

34
00:04:09.443 --> 00:04:11.977
Then be ready to.

35
00:04:16.983 --> 00:04:20.363
Are you okay? Can you hear me?

36
00:04:20.388 --> 00:04:22.254
Sir, I hope you can forgive me.

37
00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:32.241
Addison?

38
00:04:32.266 --> 00:04:35.501
Liza, get the money.

39
00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.005
Liza, now!

40
00:04:53.854 --> 00:04:56.165
See if you can get to your bag.

41
00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.367
Get anything warm.

42
00:04:58.392 --> 00:05:01.070
I'm sure that officer called for
backup, at least an ambulance.

43
00:05:01.095 --> 00:05:03.538
We can't be foolish
now, you understand?

44
00:05:03.563 --> 00:05:04.940
You have the money?

45
00:05:04.965 --> 00:05:07.108
Mm-hmm. Most of it.

46
00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:08.476
You have your health?

47
00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.078
I think so.

48
00:05:10.103 --> 00:05:12.237
Let's not dally.

49
00:05:32.925 --> 00:05:34.903
<i>Mills!</i>

50
00:05:34.928 --> 00:05:37.262
<i>Let's go. Pack it up.
You're out of here.</i>

51
00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.351
<i>You got your papers?</i>

52
00:05:49.376 --> 00:05:50.585
<i>You know how to get your
car out of impound?</i>

53
00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.420
I'm okay. Thanks.

54
00:05:52.445 --> 00:05:55.190
Going home to see your
folks for Thanksgiving?

55
00:05:55.215 --> 00:05:56.925
I don't know.

56
00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:59.183
Just let me out of here.

57
00:06:31.416 --> 00:06:33.717
<i>Hello?</i>

58
00:06:37.588 --> 00:06:39.500
<i>Hello?</i>

59
00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:41.525
Dad, it's Jay.

60
00:06:44.429 --> 00:06:46.073
<i>Dad, are you there?</i>

61
00:06:46.098 --> 00:06:48.432
Hello, son.

62
00:06:50.635 --> 00:06:53.170
How you've been?

63
00:06:55.006 --> 00:06:57.341
Decent.

64
00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.325
Listen, I'm in the
middle of something.

65
00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.283
I'll get your mother.

66
00:07:10.388 --> 00:07:12.356
<i>Who is it?</i>

67
00:07:14.292 --> 00:07:15.536
Hello?

68
00:07:15.561 --> 00:07:17.537
Mom, it's me.

69
00:07:17.562 --> 00:07:21.107
Oh! Oh, my goodness. Hi, honey!

70
00:07:21.132 --> 00:07:23.209
<i>How are you?</i>

71
00:07:23.234 --> 00:07:24.577
I'm out.

72
00:07:24.602 --> 00:07:26.079
What?

73
00:07:26.104 --> 00:07:28.114
<i>This morning. Good behavior.</i>

74
00:07:28.139 --> 00:07:31.985
Oh, my God. That's wonderful.

75
00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:35.188
<i>Then you'll be here for
Thanksgiving tomorrow?</i>

76
00:07:35.213 --> 00:07:38.614
Oh! I'll make it nice, honey,
just the way it used to be.

77
00:07:40.017 --> 00:07:41.584
How about dad?

78
00:07:46.757 --> 00:07:49.202
Your father loves you, Jay.

79
00:07:49.227 --> 00:07:52.338
<i>He just has a hard
time showing it.</i>

80
00:07:52.363 --> 00:07:55.008
Listen. If it's more
comfortable tomorrow morning,

81
00:07:55.033 --> 00:07:56.642
he'll be gone hunting.

82
00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:59.145
<i>We could talk about it then.</i>

83
00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.748
I just need the keys to the
cottage, if that's okay.

84
00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:04.150
<i>Oh, sure. They're here.
Just come and get 'em.</i>

85
00:08:04.175 --> 00:08:07.754
Do you need money?

86
00:08:07.779 --> 00:08:09.522
<i>Are you in trouble?</i>

87
00:08:09.547 --> 00:08:11.547
Mom I've got to go.

88
00:08:36.072 --> 00:08:38.406
<i>Read the sign!</i>

89
00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.228
Oh, shit.

90
00:08:50.253 --> 00:08:52.230
Jay.

91
00:08:52.255 --> 00:08:53.632
"Mohawk" mills.

92
00:08:53.657 --> 00:08:55.634
Jay.

93
00:08:55.659 --> 00:08:57.836
Just Jay.

94
00:08:57.861 --> 00:09:00.105
Time really flies by.

95
00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:02.707
It didn't fly by for me.

96
00:09:02.732 --> 00:09:05.510
Well, come on in, kid.

97
00:09:05.535 --> 00:09:08.736
Just watching some
tape on a new fighter.

98
00:09:10.806 --> 00:09:13.341
Yeah, you were really
something then.

99
00:09:15.144 --> 00:09:17.556
No one threw a
left hook harder.

100
00:09:17.581 --> 00:09:19.591
You weren't even there, Ronnie.

101
00:09:19.616 --> 00:09:22.260
How'd you end up with my medal?

102
00:09:22.285 --> 00:09:25.797
I just figured I'd hang
onto it, you know,

103
00:09:25.822 --> 00:09:27.432
for safekeeping.

104
00:09:27.457 --> 00:09:28.490
Right.

105
00:09:33.428 --> 00:09:35.729
It looks good on you, kid.

106
00:09:36.898 --> 00:09:38.876
When did you get out?

107
00:09:38.901 --> 00:09:40.511
Couple of hours ago.

108
00:09:40.536 --> 00:09:43.681
Wow, you came straight here.
I'm honored.

109
00:09:43.706 --> 00:09:45.683
Who tipped off the boxing
commission, Ronnie?

110
00:09:45.708 --> 00:09:47.551
Hell if I know.

111
00:09:47.576 --> 00:09:50.821
Well, how come I was the
only one that took the fall?

112
00:09:50.846 --> 00:09:52.623
How come you were
never indicted?

113
00:09:52.648 --> 00:09:54.158
A lot of questions.

114
00:09:54.183 --> 00:09:56.717
I had a lot of time
to think of them.

115
00:09:58.653 --> 00:10:00.498
I want the money you owe me.

116
00:10:00.523 --> 00:10:03.534
How do you figure I
owe you money, kid?

117
00:10:03.559 --> 00:10:05.703
The fucking fight, Ronnie!

118
00:10:05.728 --> 00:10:06.904
Okay, I get it.

119
00:10:06.929 --> 00:10:09.607
Remember, kid,

120
00:10:09.632 --> 00:10:12.476
you were like a son to me.

121
00:10:12.501 --> 00:10:14.912
I don't have a lot right now,

122
00:10:14.937 --> 00:10:17.781
but I've got some.

123
00:10:17.806 --> 00:10:20.507
Some's better than none, right?

124
00:10:23.711 --> 00:10:26.713
Not much, but it's all
I've got right now.

125
00:10:33.489 --> 00:10:35.566
Are you fucking stupid? You think you
can come in here and make demands?

126
00:10:35.591 --> 00:10:38.902
You're on parole! You
don't dare touch me.

127
00:10:38.927 --> 00:10:40.637
You could've been a
great fucking loser!

128
00:10:40.662 --> 00:10:42.572
We could've made a lot
of money together.

129
00:10:42.597 --> 00:10:45.398
See, the way I
figure, you owe me.

130
00:10:50.404 --> 00:10:52.738
Ronnie.

131
00:10:59.379 --> 00:11:01.714
Oh, Jesus.

132
00:11:09.823 --> 00:11:12.969
<i>9-1-1. What's your emergency?</i>

133
00:11:12.994 --> 00:11:15.238
<i>Hello?</i>

134
00:11:15.263 --> 00:11:16.973
<i>9-1-1.</i>

135
00:11:16.998 --> 00:11:18.775
<i>Is anybody there?</i>

136
00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.777
<i>Stay on the line with
me if you can hear me.</i>

137
00:11:20.802 --> 00:11:22.735
<i>We'll dispatch a car
to this address.</i>

138
00:11:26.473 --> 00:11:29.252
Jay? Hey, man!
Long time no see!

139
00:11:29.277 --> 00:11:31.287
Hey. Sorry, man.

140
00:11:31.312 --> 00:11:34.814
Jay? Hey! What's the problem?

141
00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.752
Watch it, man!

142
00:11:45.291 --> 00:11:49.771
I told Jay to stop
by tomorrow morning.

143
00:11:49.796 --> 00:11:51.997
I see.

144
00:11:53.734 --> 00:11:55.567
Don't do this, Chet.

145
00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:59.471
It's not fair.

146
00:12:01.407 --> 00:12:03.742
He turned his back
on his family.

147
00:12:09.915 --> 00:12:11.916
I wonder who that is.

148
00:12:18.024 --> 00:12:19.334
Hi, Hanna!

149
00:12:19.359 --> 00:12:21.903
Hi! Hi, sheriff mills.

150
00:12:21.928 --> 00:12:24.840
Not me. My spurs are hung. Oh!

151
00:12:24.865 --> 00:12:26.742
It's so good to see you guys.

152
00:12:26.767 --> 00:12:28.410
Seems like it's been forever.

153
00:12:28.435 --> 00:12:29.978
Look at you.

154
00:12:30.003 --> 00:12:33.682
What a pretty young
woman you turned into.

155
00:12:33.707 --> 00:12:35.851
You're the spitting
image of your mom.

156
00:12:35.876 --> 00:12:38.053
I remember my mom and dad
used to take me here.

157
00:12:38.078 --> 00:12:39.888
For Thanksgiving
when I was little.

158
00:12:39.913 --> 00:12:42.024
Jay and I used to always
feed all those leftover.

159
00:12:42.049 --> 00:12:44.493
Bones and things to that
big pig you guys had.

160
00:12:44.518 --> 00:12:46.028
Jay was always
going on about...

161
00:12:46.053 --> 00:12:48.563
Oh, uh, what brings
you out here now?

162
00:12:48.588 --> 00:12:52.767
Oh, uh, we actually
have a bad situation.

163
00:12:52.792 --> 00:12:55.303
I wanted to give you
guys a heads up.

164
00:12:55.328 --> 00:12:57.338
What do you mean by bad?

165
00:12:57.363 --> 00:12:59.740
Late last night, one
of the tribal casinos.

166
00:12:59.765 --> 00:13:01.709
Down in mt. Pleasant
was robbed.

167
00:13:01.734 --> 00:13:04.478
Two armed suspects
wearing masks...

168
00:13:04.503 --> 00:13:06.580
Anyone hurt?

169
00:13:06.605 --> 00:13:08.849
Around 6 this morning, a
state trooper came upon.

170
00:13:08.874 --> 00:13:11.052
An accident site a
ways South of us.

171
00:13:11.077 --> 00:13:13.988
When backup arrived, they found
the trooper shot to death.

172
00:13:14.013 --> 00:13:15.690
Oh, my God.

173
00:13:15.715 --> 00:13:17.758
One of the suspects
died in the crash.

174
00:13:17.783 --> 00:13:19.927
At least one more took to
the national forest here.

175
00:13:19.952 --> 00:13:22.463
We're setting up roadblocks
and sending in search teams,

176
00:13:22.488 --> 00:13:24.465
but it is possible he
could slip through,

177
00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:27.568
so we're just letting all
the families out here know.

178
00:13:27.593 --> 00:13:30.004
Well, it's a huge area.

179
00:13:30.029 --> 00:13:34.008
He'd never make it this
far north on foot.

180
00:13:34.033 --> 00:13:35.710
And the temperature's
supposed to keep dropping.

181
00:13:35.735 --> 00:13:37.945
I heard blizzard conditions.

182
00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:40.081
I'd say let him
freeze to death.

183
00:13:40.106 --> 00:13:43.006
Coyotes will find him.

184
00:14:06.029 --> 00:14:08.074
What are you looking
at, Addison?

185
00:14:08.099 --> 00:14:10.777
Pardon me.

186
00:14:10.802 --> 00:14:12.802
It's okay to look.

187
00:14:14.138 --> 00:14:16.873
Hush! The devil will hear you.

188
00:14:19.009 --> 00:14:21.020
What did I promise you
when we started this?

189
00:14:21.045 --> 00:14:23.790
That no one would get hurt.

190
00:14:23.815 --> 00:14:25.592
Well, I want you
to remember this.

191
00:14:25.617 --> 00:14:27.694
You didn't hurt anyone.

192
00:14:27.719 --> 00:14:29.929
I made the choice, and now
things are different.

193
00:14:29.954 --> 00:14:31.631
Different how?

194
00:14:31.656 --> 00:14:33.500
We're going to split up.

195
00:14:33.525 --> 00:14:34.968
They don't know
anything about you.

196
00:14:34.993 --> 00:14:36.836
You were just the distraction.

197
00:14:36.861 --> 00:14:38.405
I don't like this plan.

198
00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:40.140
I didn't ask you
if you liked it.

199
00:14:40.165 --> 00:14:41.708
We shouldn't split up! Shh!

200
00:14:41.733 --> 00:14:43.810
Listen.

201
00:14:43.835 --> 00:14:47.080
You follow that path and
then cut toward the road.

202
00:14:47.105 --> 00:14:51.618
Use your wits. Hitch a ride.
Keep heading north.

203
00:14:51.643 --> 00:14:54.754
We can still make it to
Canada, but till then,

204
00:14:54.779 --> 00:14:56.756
you don't know me anymore.

205
00:14:56.781 --> 00:14:58.792
I'm not your brother anymore,

206
00:14:58.817 --> 00:15:01.551
not until I let you
know it's okay.

207
00:15:04.021 --> 00:15:06.055
Remember how I taught you?

208
00:15:08.558 --> 00:15:10.035
Leave your phone on,

209
00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:12.093
and I'll call you
tonight, okay?

210
00:15:18.568 --> 00:15:22.147
You're my little girl. Say it.

211
00:15:22.172 --> 00:15:25.484
I'm your little girl.

212
00:15:25.509 --> 00:15:28.687
That's good.

213
00:15:28.712 --> 00:15:30.712
Here you go.

214
00:15:39.489 --> 00:15:41.490
What if you don't call?

215
00:15:42.658 --> 00:15:44.726
Well, then I'm dead.

216
00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:50.609
So do you have any plans
for Thanksgiving?

217
00:15:50.634 --> 00:15:54.112
No, just dinner. How about you?

218
00:15:54.137 --> 00:15:56.849
Any news from your mom, Hanna?

219
00:15:56.874 --> 00:15:58.150
You?

220
00:15:58.175 --> 00:16:00.786
No, sweetie. Not
in a long time.

221
00:16:00.811 --> 00:16:03.111
Well, it was really
good to see you.

222
00:16:04.547 --> 00:16:07.025
Bye. Bye.

223
00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:10.062
Oh, you should stop by
tomorrow for dinner.

224
00:16:10.087 --> 00:16:12.764
Oh, thanks. You know,

225
00:16:12.789 --> 00:16:15.766
I was going to ask my dad
if he had any plans,

226
00:16:15.791 --> 00:16:17.802
see if he wanted to do
something together.

227
00:16:17.827 --> 00:16:20.561
Okay. Bye.

228
00:16:35.243 --> 00:16:37.188
Hey, Doris! What's the word?

229
00:16:37.213 --> 00:16:39.023
The word is shit,

230
00:16:39.048 --> 00:16:41.158
and there's a big pile of it
waiting for you in the office.

231
00:16:41.183 --> 00:16:43.261
Becker? And the boys.

232
00:16:43.286 --> 00:16:45.763
Any mail come for me? A letter?

233
00:16:45.788 --> 00:16:47.598
Didn't come in yet.

234
00:16:47.623 --> 00:16:49.166
Well, let me know. Yes, ma'am.

235
00:16:49.191 --> 00:16:51.068
We'll provide manpower and
additional search support,

236
00:16:51.093 --> 00:16:52.904
along with the other counties.

237
00:16:52.929 --> 00:16:54.839
Shut the fucking door, eh?

238
00:16:54.864 --> 00:16:56.841
State k-9 teams won't be
here till late tonight,

239
00:16:56.866 --> 00:17:00.177
so we're going in this
afternoon with my dogs.

240
00:17:00.202 --> 00:17:02.113
Use your radios, use your heads.

241
00:17:02.138 --> 00:17:04.115
Everybody wears their vests.

242
00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.717
If you come upon this
guy, call it in.

243
00:17:06.742 --> 00:17:09.086
We all want to make it
home for Turkey dinner.

244
00:17:09.111 --> 00:17:10.721
Well, if you keep talking,

245
00:17:10.746 --> 00:17:12.657
I'm not going to make
it for Turkey dinner.

246
00:17:12.682 --> 00:17:13.891
Travis, this morning
while you were fucking.

247
00:17:13.916 --> 00:17:15.126
That little rat
you call a wife,

248
00:17:15.151 --> 00:17:18.029
this guy shot a
cop in the face.

249
00:17:18.054 --> 00:17:19.964
The cop's name was
Alan townsend.

250
00:17:19.989 --> 00:17:23.099
He served as a trooper
for 18 years.

251
00:17:23.124 --> 00:17:25.168
That man is dead, gone forever.

252
00:17:25.193 --> 00:17:28.071
All right. Take it easy. Sorry.

253
00:17:28.096 --> 00:17:32.609
This is the real deal, boys.
You understand?

254
00:17:32.634 --> 00:17:34.945
All right, now listen up.
Here's what we're going to do.

255
00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.314
Travis, Brice, bill, you'll
be with me heading west.

256
00:17:37.339 --> 00:17:39.316
From the accident site
toward the Lake Shore.

257
00:17:39.341 --> 00:17:41.318
The other four of you
will be led by Denny.

258
00:17:41.343 --> 00:17:43.687
You'll head east toward I-75.

259
00:17:43.712 --> 00:17:47.223
Okay? Let's get going.

