522
00:45:32.487 --> 00:45:34.564
Make me feel like a
silly old mother.

523
00:45:34.589 --> 00:45:36.889
Sure.

524
00:45:42.630 --> 00:45:46.343
I'll be home around noon,
unless I'm tracking one.

525
00:45:46.368 --> 00:45:48.311
Hey.

526
00:45:48.336 --> 00:45:50.280
Yeah?

527
00:45:50.305 --> 00:45:53.950
You've been pretty quiet this morning.
You okay?

528
00:45:53.975 --> 00:45:56.786
Yeah.

529
00:45:56.811 --> 00:46:00.590
You know, parenting isn't
easy, Chet, not for anyone.

530
00:46:00.615 --> 00:46:02.692
You make it look that way.

531
00:46:02.717 --> 00:46:05.829
Well, just because I'm better
at hiding the hard parts.

532
00:46:05.854 --> 00:46:08.821
And you're always graceful.

533
00:46:09.823 --> 00:46:13.293
In case you get hungry.

534
00:46:16.597 --> 00:46:20.410
I thought you said
your spurs were hung.

535
00:46:20.435 --> 00:46:22.602
It's better to
have and not need.

536
00:46:24.038 --> 00:46:26.883
Okay then.

537
00:46:26.908 --> 00:46:29.442
Stay warm.

538
00:46:30.744 --> 00:46:32.577
Don't tell me what to do.

539
00:46:52.465 --> 00:46:54.610
It's getting light out.

540
00:46:54.635 --> 00:46:57.079
Where are you?

541
00:46:57.104 --> 00:46:58.914
Are you still alive?

542
00:46:58.939 --> 00:47:01.016
I think I'd feel
it if you died.

543
00:47:01.041 --> 00:47:03.585
I mean, at least
I think I would.

544
00:47:03.610 --> 00:47:06.912
I feel like I just
have to keep moving.

545
00:47:08.514 --> 00:47:10.749
Addison?

546
00:47:12.619 --> 00:47:14.063
Everything's just...

547
00:47:14.088 --> 00:47:16.888
Everything's getting
so confusing.

548
00:47:19.592 --> 00:47:22.671
That guy I told you about,

549
00:47:22.696 --> 00:47:26.608
he turned out to be a real jerk.

550
00:47:26.633 --> 00:47:31.347
He just disappeared on me, so...

551
00:47:31.372 --> 00:47:33.615
I'll find another way,

552
00:47:33.640 --> 00:47:36.385
and I'll call you.

553
00:47:36.410 --> 00:47:39.887
Or you call me. Where are you?

554
00:47:39.912 --> 00:47:42.480
Okay. Bye.

555
00:48:22.154 --> 00:48:25.956
Hey! Hey!

556
00:48:28.994 --> 00:48:30.772
Hey, buddy. What's
your problem?

557
00:48:30.797 --> 00:48:33.141
I'll put you in a fucking coma!

558
00:48:33.166 --> 00:48:35.910
Drive the fuck away!

559
00:48:35.935 --> 00:48:37.512
What are you doing?

560
00:48:37.537 --> 00:48:38.846
What does it look like?

561
00:48:38.871 --> 00:48:40.148
Last night was fun
and all, but...

562
00:48:40.173 --> 00:48:41.549
But what?

563
00:48:41.574 --> 00:48:43.151
Well, it was just a game!

564
00:48:43.176 --> 00:48:44.886
That is bullshit,
and you know it.

565
00:48:44.911 --> 00:48:47.177
Do I? You don't
even know my name.

566
00:48:48.779 --> 00:48:50.557
So, tell me!

567
00:48:50.582 --> 00:48:53.216
What does it matter? I
could've been anybody.

568
00:48:54.985 --> 00:48:58.165
It matters to me.

569
00:48:58.190 --> 00:49:00.723
Why are you doing this?

570
00:49:11.802 --> 00:49:13.447
Hey, bill.

571
00:49:13.472 --> 00:49:15.015
You order breakfast?

572
00:49:15.040 --> 00:49:17.707
Come on, Travis.

573
00:49:22.012 --> 00:49:23.457
What are you doing here, Hanna?

574
00:49:23.482 --> 00:49:24.991
Becker will have your head.

575
00:49:25.016 --> 00:49:27.093
Vicky woodward is worried
about her daughter.

576
00:49:27.118 --> 00:49:29.029
Their cabin's a couple
of Miles from here.

577
00:49:29.054 --> 00:49:31.731
Where's Becker?

578
00:49:31.756 --> 00:49:33.700
Headed north about an hour ago.

579
00:49:33.725 --> 00:49:35.635
To meet with the state police.

580
00:49:35.660 --> 00:49:37.237
You want us to come with you?

581
00:49:37.262 --> 00:49:39.005
Not necessary.

582
00:49:39.030 --> 00:49:41.564
No, it probably is.

583
00:50:06.589 --> 00:50:08.868
When I was 10, I watched
my father bleed to death.

584
00:50:08.893 --> 00:50:11.871
In the weeds beside our house.

585
00:50:11.896 --> 00:50:15.040
He pulled himself across
the yard with his arms,

586
00:50:15.065 --> 00:50:17.743
screamed at me,
and then he died.

587
00:50:17.768 --> 00:50:20.779
Someone shot him.

588
00:50:20.804 --> 00:50:24.273
Want to know what I did next?

589
00:50:26.643 --> 00:50:29.955
Washed him off with
the garden hose,

590
00:50:29.980 --> 00:50:31.991
combed his hair,

591
00:50:32.016 --> 00:50:35.050
sat beside him and waited
for someone to find me.

592
00:50:38.922 --> 00:50:41.290
Who found you?

593
00:50:44.561 --> 00:50:48.073
My brother.

594
00:50:48.098 --> 00:50:51.266
He turned off the hose
and took me for a walk.

595
00:50:53.870 --> 00:50:56.171
What happened then?

596
00:50:58.207 --> 00:51:01.052
A lot of strangers at our
house, a lot of cops.

597
00:51:01.077 --> 00:51:04.011
People trying to figure
out where to put me.

598
00:51:09.017 --> 00:51:12.964
My father was a monster.

599
00:51:12.989 --> 00:51:17.058
An animal, and he
died like one.

600
00:51:25.834 --> 00:51:28.135
I'm supposed to be a grownup.

601
00:51:30.372 --> 00:51:31.883
If I was someone else,

602
00:51:31.908 --> 00:51:34.619
I could have a
husband of my own...

603
00:51:34.644 --> 00:51:38.323
Having my own babies.

604
00:51:38.348 --> 00:51:42.049
Instead I'm all messed up.

605
00:52:08.943 --> 00:52:11.855
Liza...

606
00:52:11.880 --> 00:52:14.948
My name is Liza.

607
00:52:17.184 --> 00:52:19.786
I'm Jay.

608
00:53:19.279 --> 00:53:21.223
What's the matter, Hanna?

609
00:53:21.248 --> 00:53:24.026
Why are we stopping?

610
00:53:24.051 --> 00:53:26.929
Guys, it looks like
this was left here.

611
00:53:26.954 --> 00:53:28.330
Strange, huh?

612
00:53:28.355 --> 00:53:30.889
So what?

613
00:54:30.449 --> 00:54:32.494
Becker, do you copy? Hey,
hey, what are you doing?

614
00:54:32.519 --> 00:54:35.130
I'm calling in to
Becker for backup.

615
00:54:35.155 --> 00:54:36.898
Call in what? It's a snowmobile
and a hunting cabin.

616
00:54:36.923 --> 00:54:38.433
While the two of you
have your little spat,

617
00:54:38.458 --> 00:54:40.301
I'm just going to
go and do my job.

618
00:54:40.326 --> 00:54:41.870
We have to check it out.

619
00:54:41.895 --> 00:54:43.538
Okay, fine. So we check it out,

620
00:54:43.563 --> 00:54:45.440
but don't go calling
Becker now for nothing.

621
00:54:45.465 --> 00:54:47.275
Me and Brice are the ones who
will end up in deep shit.

622
00:54:47.300 --> 00:54:50.345
Becker told us to call.
I'm calling.

623
00:54:50.370 --> 00:54:53.314
Becker, do you copy?

624
00:54:53.339 --> 00:54:55.316
What the hell? You
can't do that!

625
00:54:55.341 --> 00:54:57.341
Can't do what?

626
00:54:58.877 --> 00:55:01.512
Such an asshole.

627
00:55:07.252 --> 00:55:09.464
Hello! Bobby?

628
00:55:09.489 --> 00:55:12.200
Hello!

629
00:55:12.225 --> 00:55:14.492
This is the sheriff's office.
Hello!

630
00:55:19.431 --> 00:55:21.509
You're going to get
us in trouble, Hanna.

631
00:55:21.534 --> 00:55:23.144
I know it's early.

632
00:55:23.169 --> 00:55:25.469
We'd just like to
have a quick word.

633
00:55:29.374 --> 00:55:31.875
Oh, my God.

634
00:55:34.111 --> 00:55:36.456
Hello!

635
00:55:36.481 --> 00:55:41.218
Brice! Get away! It's him!

636
00:55:42.955 --> 00:55:44.998
Brice?

637
00:55:45.023 --> 00:55:46.934
You're no angel at all.

638
00:55:46.959 --> 00:55:50.204
No, I am not.

639
00:55:50.229 --> 00:55:52.963
Brice, you all right?

640
00:55:54.166 --> 00:55:56.466
Hanna, get down!

641
00:56:02.406 --> 00:56:04.941
Come on!

642
00:56:16.020 --> 00:56:18.355
Oh, fuck!

643
00:57:21.551 --> 00:57:23.596
Are you all right?

644
00:57:23.621 --> 00:57:26.155
You're not even supposed
to be here, Hanna!

645
00:57:28.325 --> 00:57:32.027
God damn it, Travis!

646
00:58:18.741 --> 00:58:21.275
Travis!

647
00:59:08.823 --> 00:59:11.568
You know, this is
my first snowman?

648
00:59:11.593 --> 00:59:13.470
You're shitting me.

649
00:59:13.495 --> 00:59:16.673
Not a lot of snow in Alabama.

650
00:59:16.698 --> 00:59:19.243
One night when I was a kid,

651
00:59:19.268 --> 00:59:21.078
the northern lights were out,

652
00:59:21.103 --> 00:59:23.147
and my dad and I made these
snowmen out in the pasture.

653
00:59:23.172 --> 00:59:25.115
Like a boxing match,

654
00:59:25.140 --> 00:59:28.652
two snow fighters
throwing punches.

655
00:59:28.677 --> 00:59:31.622
I remember I didn't want
to go to bed that night.

656
00:59:31.647 --> 00:59:34.714
My dad carried me all the
way back to the house.

657
00:59:40.321 --> 00:59:44.668
When I got down off the
podium in Beijing,

658
00:59:44.693 --> 00:59:47.627
he was so fucking proud of me.

659
00:59:50.264 --> 00:59:52.309
And then later in
the dressing room,

660
00:59:52.334 --> 00:59:54.378
I told him I was leaving
home to go pro.

661
00:59:54.403 --> 00:59:56.547
I said to him...

662
00:59:56.572 --> 01:00:00.806
I said if I had a real coach,
maybe I'd won the gold.

663
01:00:04.811 --> 01:00:08.157
He still love you?

664
01:00:08.182 --> 01:00:10.393
Yeah, I guess, but...

665
01:00:10.418 --> 01:00:13.329
Well, you're lucky.

666
01:00:13.354 --> 01:00:15.654
You should see him.

667
01:00:25.398 --> 01:00:28.644
If I was going to see him,

668
01:00:28.669 --> 01:00:31.303
I'd like to introduce you.

669
01:00:33.807 --> 01:00:37.820
It's Thanksgiving. That's
standard procedure.

670
01:00:37.845 --> 01:00:40.513
You don't want me
there, Jay, seriously.

671
01:00:42.182 --> 01:00:44.517
I seriously do.

672
01:00:48.555 --> 01:00:51.501
What about Patricia? Isn't
she going to be there?

673
01:00:51.526 --> 01:00:53.169
Who?

674
01:00:53.194 --> 01:00:56.472
Now, don't tell me
there's no Patricia.

675
01:00:56.497 --> 01:00:59.532
Who is she to you?

676
01:01:04.638 --> 01:01:06.871
I'd rather not talk about her.

677
01:01:09.175 --> 01:01:12.287
It's kind of personal.

678
01:01:12.312 --> 01:01:16.424
I think I've told you some
personal things, Jay.

679
01:01:16.449 --> 01:01:18.693
Miss December.

680
01:01:18.718 --> 01:01:20.162
What?

681
01:01:20.187 --> 01:01:21.596
Patricia is miss December.

682
01:01:21.621 --> 01:01:24.633
Playboy, Christmas issue.

683
01:01:24.658 --> 01:01:28.370
She's a centerfold?

684
01:01:28.395 --> 01:01:30.461
A nudie picture?

685
01:01:33.633 --> 01:01:36.878
Did you two have a
meaningful relationship?

686
01:01:36.903 --> 01:01:40.282
We did. She was
very understanding,

687
01:01:40.307 --> 01:01:42.250
not too demanding.

688
01:01:42.275 --> 01:01:45.554
And were you faithful
to her, Jay?

689
01:01:45.579 --> 01:01:48.657
I was. She was my one and only.

690
01:01:48.682 --> 01:01:51.583
She never let me down.

691
01:01:54.220 --> 01:01:56.798
Hey, lovebirds!

692
01:01:56.823 --> 01:01:58.833
Roads are open!

693
01:01:58.858 --> 01:02:01.770
And to answer your question,
she probably won't be.

694
01:02:01.795 --> 01:02:04.539
At Thanksgiving dinner
at my parents' house.

695
01:02:04.564 --> 01:02:06.731
Good. Bitch better stay clear.

696
01:02:58.349 --> 01:03:00.861
Guys!

697
01:03:00.886 --> 01:03:02.997
Dad, I think I shot him.

698
01:03:03.022 --> 01:03:06.533
I think he's wounded.

699
01:03:06.558 --> 01:03:08.802
He's wearing a buckskin jacket.

700
01:03:08.827 --> 01:03:12.573
With a blackbird or an eagle...

701
01:03:12.598 --> 01:03:13.741
At least I think it's
an eagle on the back...

702
01:03:13.766 --> 01:03:14.808
Just shut your mouth.

703
01:03:14.833 --> 01:03:17.745
Dad! I said shut your mouth!

704
01:03:17.770 --> 01:03:20.813
I told you to stay
out of the woods!

705
01:03:20.838 --> 01:03:23.416
You see what happens when
you stick your nose in?

706
01:03:23.441 --> 01:03:25.551
People start dying!

707
01:03:25.576 --> 01:03:28.721
Where's Travis?

708
01:03:28.746 --> 01:03:32.925
A field, about 10 Miles west.

709
01:03:32.950 --> 01:03:35.484
He's dead?

710
01:03:38.689 --> 01:03:40.033
If you were one of my boys,

711
01:03:40.058 --> 01:03:42.802
I would hit you
so fucking hard.

712
01:03:42.827 --> 01:03:46.095
If I were one of your boys,
you'd be proud of me.

713
01:03:48.399 --> 01:03:50.610
I want everybody the
hell out of here.

714
01:03:50.635 --> 01:03:52.345
All of you. You hear me?

715
01:03:52.370 --> 01:03:54.704
Well, I can help... all of you!

716
01:03:56.940 --> 01:03:59.475
Shut up!

717
01:04:39.815 --> 01:04:41.793
Chester mills, you'd
better not be.

718
01:04:41.818 --> 01:04:43.028
Walking in here
with your boots...

719
01:04:43.053 --> 01:04:44.896
Shh.

720
01:04:44.921 --> 01:04:46.932
What's your name?

721
01:04:46.957 --> 01:04:49.534
June.

722
01:04:49.559 --> 01:04:52.494
June, put that pan
down, please.

723
01:05:00.936 --> 01:05:03.815
Is there anyone else
in the house, June?

724
01:05:03.840 --> 01:05:05.817
No.

725
01:05:05.842 --> 01:05:08.843
Step down and take a seat.

726
01:05:11.514 --> 01:05:13.759
Who might come home, June?

727
01:05:13.784 --> 01:05:18.930
My husband, Chet.

728
01:05:18.955 --> 01:05:20.799
Where is he?

729
01:05:20.824 --> 01:05:22.134
Deer hunting.

730
01:05:22.159 --> 01:05:24.035
He'll be armed?

731
01:05:24.060 --> 01:05:28.062
With a rifle.

732
01:05:37.705 --> 01:05:39.784
Why are you so calm?

733
01:05:39.809 --> 01:05:43.644
A panicking woman is
no help to anyone.

734
01:05:47.982 --> 01:05:49.794
I like you, June.

735
01:05:49.819 --> 01:05:53.554
You do as I say, and I won't
hurt you or your family.

736
01:05:54.556 --> 01:05:56.690
Thank you.

737
01:06:08.470 --> 01:06:10.737
Would you mind op...

738
01:06:12.040 --> 01:06:14.675
Opening a window, please?

739
01:06:50.244 --> 01:06:52.021
May I take a look at that?

740
01:06:52.046 --> 01:06:55.091
Are you my mother?

741
01:06:55.116 --> 01:06:58.784
Somebody's mother.

742
01:07:22.175 --> 01:07:24.710
Ah, shit!

743
01:07:25.812 --> 01:07:27.624
You'll live.

744
01:07:27.649 --> 01:07:29.592
Well, that remains to
be determined, June,

745
01:07:29.617 --> 01:07:31.951
but thank you.

746
01:07:34.321 --> 01:07:36.733
Do not turn around.

747
01:07:36.758 --> 01:07:39.736
Do exactly what I say.

748
01:07:39.761 --> 01:07:43.206
Slowly put your hands on your
head, interlocking your fingers.

749
01:07:43.231 --> 01:07:45.975
To do that, I'd have
to take my hand.

750
01:07:46.000 --> 01:07:50.646
Off the gun I have pointed
at June on the table...

751
01:07:50.671 --> 01:07:52.614
Which isn't going to happen.

752
01:07:52.639 --> 01:07:54.917
He will shoot you, kiddo.

753
01:07:54.942 --> 01:07:56.985
I don't think he will.

754
01:07:57.010 --> 01:07:59.087
Don't try me, son.

755
01:07:59.112 --> 01:08:00.946
No. He has too much to lose.

756
01:08:03.149 --> 01:08:06.952
Sir, believe me when I say
that I genuinely like June.

757
01:08:08.721 --> 01:08:13.058
So, for both of us, would
you please back down?

758
01:08:18.297 --> 01:08:20.342
God damn it.

759
01:08:20.367 --> 01:08:23.134
Open the rifle action and
put the gun on the floor.

760
01:08:28.841 --> 01:08:31.610
Take a seat beside your wife.

761
01:08:33.980 --> 01:08:36.058
I'm sorry.

762
01:08:36.083 --> 01:08:38.126
Nothing to be sorry for.

763
01:08:38.151 --> 01:08:41.029
Chet, is it? How
was the hunting?

764
01:08:41.054 --> 01:08:45.968
You know, when I was a kid, we
had a Springfield 20 gauge.

765
01:08:45.993 --> 01:08:50.061
We used to hunt
ducks and coons.

766
01:08:56.168 --> 01:08:58.669
You bake pies from
scratch, June?

767
01:09:00.171 --> 01:09:01.849
For Thanksgiving, I do.

768
01:09:01.874 --> 01:09:04.251
Oh, that's right.

769
01:09:04.276 --> 01:09:07.989
It's Thanksgiving.

770
01:09:08.014 --> 01:09:10.091
Would it be all right.

771
01:09:10.116 --> 01:09:12.383
If we went ahead
and served dinner?

772
01:09:14.152 --> 01:09:17.264
It would be really nice
to have a good meal.

773
01:09:17.289 --> 01:09:19.000
Are you out of
your fucking mind?

774
01:09:19.025 --> 01:09:20.334
I would like that.

775
01:09:20.359 --> 01:09:21.869
Honey...

776
01:09:21.894 --> 01:09:23.838
Chet, we have to eat.
It will occupy us.

777
01:09:23.863 --> 01:09:26.140
Keep things from
getting too crazy.

778
01:09:26.165 --> 01:09:27.642
Thank you, June.

779
01:09:27.667 --> 01:09:29.276
Don't thank me. Chet
shot the goose.

780
01:09:29.301 --> 01:09:32.202
Well, thank you, Chet.

781
01:09:37.042 --> 01:09:38.853
What are you looking for?

782
01:09:38.878 --> 01:09:41.389
Nothing. I'm just, uh...

783
01:09:41.414 --> 01:09:44.114
Wondering if the police
are waiting for you?

784
01:09:45.984 --> 01:09:48.819
I know what people are like
when they're on the run.

785
01:09:54.693 --> 01:09:57.438
I fucked up.

786
01:09:57.463 --> 01:10:01.342
It wasn't my fault, but...

787
01:10:01.367 --> 01:10:05.145
I'm not going back to prison.

788
01:10:05.170 --> 01:10:08.137
I can't.

789
01:10:20.918 --> 01:10:23.252
Is it safe?

790
01:10:26.423 --> 01:10:28.725
Who's that, June?

791
01:10:33.163 --> 01:10:35.041
Oh, my God. It's our son.

792
01:10:35.066 --> 01:10:37.366
It's Jay.

793
01:10:42.506 --> 01:10:45.041
Well, well, well.

794
01:10:49.880 --> 01:10:52.482
Be careful. The steps are icy.

795
01:10:54.985 --> 01:10:56.329
Hey, mom.

796
01:10:56.354 --> 01:10:59.065
Jay. Oh, Jay.

797
01:10:59.090 --> 01:11:02.068
I brought a guest.

798
01:11:02.093 --> 01:11:04.204
Oh, Jay. Listen to me.

799
01:11:04.229 --> 01:11:07.096
There's a man in our
house, and he has a gun.

800
01:11:08.932 --> 01:11:11.077
Don't. Don't do anything.

801
01:11:11.102 --> 01:11:12.945
He'll hurt your dad.

802
01:11:12.970 --> 01:11:15.771
Please just come
in, both of you.

803
01:11:20.176 --> 01:11:22.054
Dad, you okay?

804
01:11:22.079 --> 01:11:24.523
I'm okay, son.

805
01:11:24.548 --> 01:11:26.325
Good afternoon.

806
01:11:26.350 --> 01:11:28.360
You must be Jay.

807
01:11:28.385 --> 01:11:29.895
What do you want?

808
01:11:29.920 --> 01:11:32.331
This must be your wife.

809
01:11:32.356 --> 01:11:34.890
She's my friend.

810
01:11:36.225 --> 01:11:38.904
Well, I think the lady
can speak for herself.

811
01:11:38.929 --> 01:11:40.472
What's your name?

812
01:11:40.497 --> 01:11:43.008
Liza.

813
01:11:43.033 --> 01:11:44.309
Liza.

814
01:11:44.334 --> 01:11:45.944
Well, that's a nice name.

815
01:11:45.969 --> 01:11:48.303
Take a seat.

816
01:11:52.208 --> 01:11:54.920
Both of you.

817
01:11:54.945 --> 01:11:56.155
The goose should be done soon.

818
01:11:56.180 --> 01:11:58.791
Is that correct, June? Yes.

819
01:11:58.816 --> 01:12:01.583
Great. I don't know about
you all, but I'm famished.

820
01:12:05.454 --> 01:12:07.332
Chet, here.

821
01:12:07.357 --> 01:12:10.903
Have some wine. Take
it away from me.

822
01:12:10.928 --> 01:12:14.072
It's going straight to my head.

823
01:12:14.097 --> 01:12:17.075
I need some food, and
I need some sleep.

824
01:12:17.100 --> 01:12:19.400
Besides, it's Thanksgiving.

825
01:12:25.507 --> 01:12:28.442
Are you testing me, Jay?

826
01:12:34.449 --> 01:12:37.017
Because that would
be a terrible idea.

827
01:13:09.985 --> 01:13:11.629
<i>This is sheriff t. Becker,</i>

828
01:13:11.654 --> 01:13:15.266
<i>requesting the state
police crime scene unit...</i>

829
01:13:15.291 --> 01:13:17.335
<i>And be advised we're
losing daylight.</i>

830
01:13:17.360 --> 01:13:20.905
<i>And must stay on the
suspect's trail.</i>

831
01:13:20.930 --> 01:13:23.564
Happy Thanksgiving, mom.

832
01:13:33.007 --> 01:13:34.985
Hello.

833
01:13:35.010 --> 01:13:38.588
Yeah, this is the sheriff's office.
Hanna Becker speaking.

834
01:13:38.613 --> 01:13:41.147
Sure.

835
01:13:43.584 --> 01:13:47.520
Detective Frank Mac,
Detroit police department.

836
01:13:51.025 --> 01:13:53.536
Say that again?

837
01:13:53.561 --> 01:13:57.964
Oh, yeah. I know the family.
I know where they live.

838
01:14:00.534 --> 01:14:04.447
A concussion? So you
need his statement.

839
01:14:04.472 --> 01:14:06.983
Got it.

840
01:14:07.008 --> 01:14:09.542
I'll go over there.
I'll let you know.

841
01:14:11.412 --> 01:14:13.446
Happy holiday to you, too.

842
01:14:16.483 --> 01:14:19.052
Jesus Christ.

843
01:14:24.391 --> 01:14:26.503
June, do you say grace
at Thanksgiving?

844
01:14:26.528 --> 01:14:28.405
We give thanks.

845
01:14:28.430 --> 01:14:30.407
And how does that work?

846
01:14:30.432 --> 01:14:34.476
We all go around and say
something we're thankful for.

847
01:14:34.501 --> 01:14:37.346
An excellent idea.

848
01:14:37.371 --> 01:14:39.415
Would you mind starting?

849
01:14:39.440 --> 01:14:41.740
Please?

850
01:14:46.112 --> 01:14:48.958
I'm thankful for this food,

851
01:14:48.983 --> 01:14:52.494
for God's charity,

852
01:14:52.519 --> 01:14:55.164
and for giving me his
two greatest men,

853
01:14:55.189 --> 01:14:57.499
my husband and my son.

854
01:14:57.524 --> 01:15:00.092
Well said.

855
01:15:01.461 --> 01:15:05.040
Chet? You're next.

856
01:15:05.065 --> 01:15:08.266
I'm thankful for June,
the love of my life.

857
01:15:10.370 --> 01:15:13.382
Wow, that was sweet, Chet!

858
01:15:13.407 --> 01:15:15.574
How about your son?

859
01:15:18.044 --> 01:15:20.712
What's wrong with him, hmm?

860
01:15:24.317 --> 01:15:26.261
Let's ask him.

861
01:15:26.286 --> 01:15:29.031
Jay, what are you grateful for?

862
01:15:29.056 --> 01:15:31.400
It's none of your
fucking business.

863
01:15:31.425 --> 01:15:34.036
No, you're missing
the point, Jay.

864
01:15:34.061 --> 01:15:36.338
Well, I'm not going
to give you anything.

865
01:15:36.363 --> 01:15:39.041
Jay, it's your turn.
Addison, please stop.

866
01:15:39.066 --> 01:15:41.065
These people haven't
done anything to you.

867
01:15:45.404 --> 01:15:47.582
You best watch your
mouth, little girl.

868
01:15:47.607 --> 01:15:50.541
Don't you forget
where you belong.

869
01:15:54.212 --> 01:15:56.357
Give thanks, Jay.

870
01:15:56.382 --> 01:15:59.093
You'd better say something
I know you really mean.

871
01:15:59.118 --> 01:16:02.030
You think I'm afraid of you?

872
01:16:02.055 --> 01:16:03.531
Look at you.

873
01:16:03.556 --> 01:16:05.056
You're nothing
without that gun.

874
01:16:08.727 --> 01:16:11.572
What if this is your daddy's
last moment of life?

875
01:16:11.597 --> 01:16:13.775
What do you want him
to take with him?

876
01:16:13.800 --> 01:16:17.368
Jay. Please, honey.

877
01:16:22.541 --> 01:16:25.686
I'm sorry, dad.

878
01:16:25.711 --> 01:16:28.245
I messed everything up so bad.

879
01:16:30.682 --> 01:16:33.661
That fight, they told
me it was the only way.

880
01:16:33.686 --> 01:16:36.587
They'd give me a
shot at the title.

881
01:16:39.191 --> 01:16:42.437
I laid down.

882
01:16:42.462 --> 01:16:45.096
I let 'em beat me.

883
01:16:47.732 --> 01:16:50.433
I don't deserve to be
sitting here at your table.

884
01:16:58.142 --> 01:17:00.477
This is your table, son.

885
01:17:03.747 --> 01:17:08.585
And you're not the only
one who messed up.

886
01:17:35.412 --> 01:17:37.491
Once again, June,

887
01:17:37.516 --> 01:17:40.727
the goose was really
quite wonderful.

888
01:17:40.752 --> 01:17:42.829
What are you going to do?

889
01:17:42.854 --> 01:17:45.665
I'm going to have
some more red wine.

890
01:17:45.690 --> 01:17:48.702
I'm going to have some more
of your wife's homemade pie.

891
01:17:48.727 --> 01:17:51.571
About the police?

892
01:17:51.596 --> 01:17:53.306
I don't know, Chet.

893
01:17:53.331 --> 01:17:54.771
I feel pretty good
just sitting here.

894
01:17:59.703 --> 01:18:02.181
Hey, it's Hanna.

895
01:18:02.206 --> 01:18:04.683
Hanna Becker.

896
01:18:04.708 --> 01:18:06.685
We know that officer.

897
01:18:06.710 --> 01:18:08.454
She's a friend of the family.

898
01:18:08.479 --> 01:18:11.780
Just dropping by
on Thanksgiving?

899
01:18:13.816 --> 01:18:15.161
I invited her.

900
01:18:15.186 --> 01:18:16.852
That slip your mind, June?

901
01:18:19.323 --> 01:18:20.722
Ask her in.

902
01:18:23.493 --> 01:18:24.637
No.

903
01:18:24.662 --> 01:18:27.773
Do it.

904
01:18:27.798 --> 01:18:30.332
Come on in, Hanna.

905
01:18:31.801 --> 01:18:33.879
Hey, everybody.
Sorry to interrupt.

906
01:18:33.904 --> 01:18:35.581
I don't think you know everyone.
This is...

907
01:18:35.606 --> 01:18:37.773
I'm the killer.

908
01:18:39.976 --> 01:18:41.720
I'm the one you're
all looking for.

909
01:18:41.745 --> 01:18:43.756
I'm sorry, Hanna.

910
01:18:43.781 --> 01:18:45.858
I didn't know what to do.

911
01:18:45.883 --> 01:18:47.526
I wouldn't either.

912
01:18:47.551 --> 01:18:49.851
Give me your belt.

913
01:18:55.558 --> 01:18:57.960
Take a seat.

914
01:18:59.395 --> 01:19:00.739
Go on.

915
01:19:00.764 --> 01:19:05.210
June, would you please
serve some pie?

916
01:19:05.235 --> 01:19:08.580
Do you want pumpkin or apple?

917
01:19:08.605 --> 01:19:10.481
I'm going to have pumpkin.

918
01:19:10.506 --> 01:19:12.773
Seems more appropriate
for the holidays.

919
01:19:14.276 --> 01:19:18.790
So, Hanna, what are you doing here?
Thank you.

920
01:19:18.815 --> 01:19:20.892
It's Thanksgiving.

921
01:19:20.917 --> 01:19:23.995
Don't you got anybody
of your own?

922
01:19:24.020 --> 01:19:27.398
I'm here for Jay.

923
01:19:27.423 --> 01:19:30.835
Hey. Long time.

924
01:19:30.860 --> 01:19:32.637
Yeah.

925
01:19:32.662 --> 01:19:35.907
I got a call from a
detective in Detroit.

926
01:19:35.932 --> 01:19:37.642
He needs to talk with you.

927
01:19:37.667 --> 01:19:40.511
Oops. In trouble with
the police, Jay?

928
01:19:40.536 --> 01:19:43.815
That's kind of embarrassing
for your folks.

929
01:19:43.840 --> 01:19:46.951
I mean, this all seems
pretty wholesome.

930
01:19:46.976 --> 01:19:49.787
What went wrong, buddy?

931
01:19:49.812 --> 01:19:53.992
What are they after you for?
I'm dying to know.

932
01:19:54.017 --> 01:19:57.018
I have something I'd
like to give thanks for.

933
01:20:00.422 --> 01:20:01.899
What's that?

934
01:20:01.924 --> 01:20:04.425
My brother.

935
01:20:07.062 --> 01:20:08.840
Why?

936
01:20:08.865 --> 01:20:11.308
Because when we were
little, he protected me.

937
01:20:11.333 --> 01:20:13.867
When I couldn't protect myself.

938
01:20:16.304 --> 01:20:17.781
I was so young.

939
01:20:17.806 --> 01:20:19.886
He thinks I can't remember,
but I remember all of it.

940
01:20:21.842 --> 01:20:25.578
The sound of the gun,
the blood on my shoe.

941
01:20:27.648 --> 01:20:30.027
My brother killed the devil.

942
01:20:30.052 --> 01:20:34.598
He saved me from hell, and
I am forever thankful.

943
01:20:34.623 --> 01:20:37.624
I love him so much for it.

944
01:20:41.962 --> 01:20:45.865
But now, I need a chance.

945
01:20:47.601 --> 01:20:50.080
I need a chance at my own life,

946
01:20:50.105 --> 01:20:54.017
and I want my
brother's blessing.

947
01:20:54.042 --> 01:20:59.946
I need him to please let me go.

948
01:21:27.941 --> 01:21:30.642
Eat.

949
01:21:35.048 --> 01:21:37.583
Eat!

950
01:22:17.123 --> 01:22:19.658
You two in love?

951
01:22:23.163 --> 01:22:25.696
You think he loves you?

952
01:22:30.202 --> 01:22:33.538
Do you think he loves you?

953
01:22:35.841 --> 01:22:38.787
Look at me.

954
01:22:38.812 --> 01:22:41.456
Look at me!

955
01:22:41.481 --> 01:22:43.915
Don't fucking touch her! Sit!

956
01:22:48.720 --> 01:22:51.022
You put your hand on the
table where I can see it.

957
01:22:54.994 --> 01:22:56.571
Stop it! Stop it!

958
01:22:56.596 --> 01:22:59.630
Sit down! Sit, June, sit!

959
01:23:02.134 --> 01:23:03.611
God damn you to hell.

960
01:23:03.636 --> 01:23:06.147
Addison, please. Come on.

961
01:23:06.172 --> 01:23:07.982
Let's just go, just you and me.

962
01:23:08.007 --> 01:23:09.717
No, baby. Come on. Let's go right now.
Come on.

963
01:23:09.742 --> 01:23:11.453
We're way past that now.
I'm your little girl.

964
01:23:11.478 --> 01:23:14.522
No. Please.

965
01:23:14.547 --> 01:23:16.791
Did you fuck her, Jay? Did you?

966
01:23:16.816 --> 01:23:18.827
You think he cares about you?

967
01:23:18.852 --> 01:23:21.062
You look at your boyfriend now.

968
01:23:21.087 --> 01:23:22.831
Look at him!

969
01:23:22.856 --> 01:23:25.567
Please, God, no! You
look at your family.

970
01:23:25.592 --> 01:23:27.836
You look what you've done! Huh?

971
01:23:27.861 --> 01:23:30.805
<i>This is sheriff t. Becker
requesting immediate backup.</i>

972
01:23:30.830 --> 01:23:35.242
<i>I'm going into the old mills farm,
mills farm road off county line 55.</i>

973
01:23:35.267 --> 01:23:37.644
<i>Possible manhunt
suspect on premises,</i>

974
01:23:37.669 --> 01:23:40.614
<i>described as wearing
a deerskin jacket.</i>

975
01:23:40.639 --> 01:23:43.617
With eagle emblem,
possibly wounded.

976
01:23:43.642 --> 01:23:45.986
<i>Copy that. Units en route.</i>

977
01:23:46.011 --> 01:23:47.611
<i>Be advised not to
engage until backup...</i>

978
01:25:02.652 --> 01:25:05.298
Daddy! The living room.

979
01:25:05.323 --> 01:25:07.856
Happy Thanksgiving.

980
01:25:09.693 --> 01:25:11.160
I'm glad you could make it.

981
01:25:15.266 --> 01:25:17.933
Please don't!

982
01:25:19.103 --> 01:25:20.703
No!

983
01:25:49.698 --> 01:25:52.033
Jay!

984
01:25:54.203 --> 01:25:57.105
Please! Please.

985
01:26:03.178 --> 01:26:05.713
He's my brother.

986
01:26:20.396 --> 01:26:22.864
Do you love her, Jay?

987
01:26:25.368 --> 01:26:27.902
Do you love her, Jay?

988
01:26:31.740 --> 01:26:34.409
Yes, I do.

989
01:27:10.478 --> 01:27:12.846
Addison...

990
01:27:17.019 --> 01:27:21.131
Get him out of here!

991
01:27:21.156 --> 01:27:24.134
Ma'am, I need you to get back.

992
01:27:24.159 --> 01:27:27.037
Please. I need you to get back.
Ma'am...

993
01:27:27.062 --> 01:27:29.406
Get an ambulance!

994
01:27:29.431 --> 01:27:31.498
Come on. That's it.

995
01:27:39.741 --> 01:27:41.885
That other officer, the
sheriff, wasn't wearing a vest.

996
01:27:41.910 --> 01:27:43.387
He's in rough shape.

997
01:27:43.412 --> 01:27:45.312
Do you know who his
next of kin is?

998
01:27:59.327 --> 01:28:02.228
<i>What would heaven look like?</i>

999
01:28:03.897 --> 01:28:06.409
<i>I don't know.</i>

1000
01:28:06.434 --> 01:28:10.770
<i>A farmhouse in the
valley, I guess,</i>

1001
01:28:10.772 --> 01:28:14.306
<i>like the one we grew
up in, Liza and I.</i>
